# swarm-comms-netsim.suite — the swarm-comms flows that need a real network:
# F5 (fallback paths: LAN, Tor, back to LAN), the VM form of F6 (a swarm that
# forms by itself across a LAN, a second subnet and a container bridge), M7
# (a peer that moves to a new subnet), M9 (Tor restarts under a running node)
# and M10 (no bridge or link-local endpoint advertised), with tor-link,
# nat-punch, gateway-relay and nearby-* (operator decision D11, 2026-11-20).
# The companion of swarm-comms.suite.
#
# Every world is a VM world, one at a time: each destroyer below forks a world
# that replays bootstrap-user-software-key and adopt-node, so this suite is
# many VM worlds' worth of time. tor-link and nat-punch run in separate
# worlds (tor-link's leave-lan downs node2's LAN interface, which nat-punch's
# enter-nat needs); the planner forks the second destroyer.
#
# Green (D11): 3 runs or a recorded waiver.
#
# Agent forms: tor-link alone ships a prompt.md. The operator sits on node1
# and holds no node token:
# - F5 swarm-fallback-paths judges the queries node2 sends node1 and node2's
#   log stream;
# - F6 swarm-forms-and-finds claims node2 and the reflector with
#   user.bootstrap, which a node answers to a local caller only;
# - M7 endpoint-change-relink watches node1 from before its move, which
#   move-subnet makes 30 s after the op, and closes on every node the links
#   the move left dead.

bootstrap-user-software-key
adopt-node

# F5 fallback paths
swarm-fallback-paths
tor-restart-onion               # M9
tor-link
nat-punch
gateway-relay

# M7 a peer moves
endpoint-change-swarm
endpoint-change-relink
endpoint-change-double

# F6 forms and finds
swarm-forms-and-finds
endpoints-advertised-clean      # M10
nearby-adopt
nearby-stealth-meet
nearby-silent
nearby-relink
nearby-join
nearby-adopt-ports
nearby-stealth-meet-ports
